KZ2 patch 6058: the texture cache's size is a run-time setting (LD_TEX_CACHE_ENTRIES, 1024..32768; default 8,192 as
before), and [tex-hash] says why textures are new: entries in use / size, local video memory, new entries, re-adds of
evicted keys and the guest-write scans that walk every entry (Fable frame plan 2026-11-03 step 1a).

Fable's step 1a: in Corinth Sands' heavy outdoor view the 8,192-entry cache was full and its LRU recycled ~365
textures per frame ([tex-hash] evict=93.6k per 256 frames, 8,298 new decodes/s), so make it 32,768. Measured here
(3 rotated pairs of the same exe, LD_TEX_CACHE_ENTRIES=8192 against 32768, LD_NO_PRESENT=1, the RE notes
"An earlier change"): 32,768 entries also fill up and keep evicting (~6,000 a second in the heavy view), new decodes fall ~20 %
while their time does not (the textures' content is new: in-place refreshes rise as evictions fall), and the frame
gets slower (heavy view 19.4/19.0/27.5 -> 15.0/14.2/24.3 fps). So the default stays 8,192. What changed:
- MAX_TEXTURES (the arrays: g.textures, the LRU links, the hash index, the CPU SRV heap's texture slots) is 32,768;
  the cache is full at g_ld_tex_cap (LD_TEX_CACHE_ENTRIES=N, default LD_TEX_CACHE_DEFAULT 8,192). Host memory ~4 MB.
- [tex-hash] adds entries=N/cap, vram= (IDXGIAdapter3::QueryVideoMemoryInfo, local segment CurrentUsage, MB), new=
  (new entries) and readd= (new entries whose key had been evicted: a direct-mapped table of evicted key hashes,
  64 Ki slots; re-adds near new= mean the cache is too small, few mean the keys are new and no size helps), and
  gvmark=N/Sk (rsx_live_draw_note_guest_write and ld_gv_mark calls and the entries they walked: both walk every entry,
  which is why a larger cache costs time).

